---
layout: base.njk
title: Home
description: Personal static blog about the permaweb, by biru25. Built with Eleventy and deployed to Arweave.
---
<section class="hero">
    <span class="chip">Stored permanently on Arweave</span>
    <h1>
        Notes from the <span class="gradient">permaweb</span>.
    </h1>
    <p class="lead">
        {{ site.tagline }}
    </p>
    <div class="cta-row">
        <a href="/blog/" class="btn btn-primary">Read the blog</a>
        <a href="/about/" class="btn btn-ghost">About me</a>
    </div>
</section>

<section class="latest">
    <h2>Latest posts</h2>
    <ul class="post-list">
        {% for post in collections.post | reverse %}
            <li>
                <a href="{{ post.url }}" class="post-link">
                    <span class="post-date">{{ post.date | readableDate }}</span>
                    <span class="post-title">{{ post.data.title }}</span>
                    <span class="post-summary">{{ post.data.summary }}</span>
                </a>
            </li>
        {% endfor %}
    </ul>
</section>

<section class="why">
    <h2>Why static on Arweave?</h2>
    <div class="why-grid">
        <div>
            <h3>1. No server to maintain</h3>
            <p>Eleventy renders all pages at build time. The output is just HTML -- AR.IO gateways can serve it directly.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
            <h3>2. Permanent by design</h3>
            <p>Once uploaded, every post becomes an Arweave transaction. It cannot be deleted, edited, or censored.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
            <h3>3. Fast &amp; cheap</h3>
            <p>Static files are tiny. Uploading via Turbo SDK is free for files under 100 KiB.</p>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>
